#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:14
msgid "`-cir-call-conv-lowering`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16
msgid "_Lower CIR function signatures and call sites to match target ABI_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:18
msgid ""
"This pass rewrites `cir.func` signatures and `cir.call` sites to match the "
"target ABI's calling convention requirements (extension attributes, struct "
"coercion, sret/byval indirect passing, struct flattening, etc.)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:22
msgid "Requirements on the input IR:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:24
msgid ""
"All C++-specific CIR types must already be lowered to ABI-relevant shapes.  "
"In particular, member pointers and method types must have been rewritten by "
"`CXXABILowering` so that the pass sees only the final ABI representation of "
"each value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:28
msgid ""
"The module must carry a `dlti.dl_spec` attribute so the classifier can query "
"type sizes and alignments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:31
msgid "Two driver modes select how each function's classification is computed:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:33
msgid ""
"`target=<name>` selects an ABI target.  The clang pipeline picks the target "
"from the module triple.  Supported targets:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:35
msgid "`\"x86_64\"`: System V."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:36
msgid "`\"amdgpu\"`: AMDGPU."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:37
msgid ""
"`\"test\"`: the MLIR test target in `mlir/lib/ABI/Targets/Test/`. Other "
"targets will be added as the LLVM ABI library ships them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:39
msgid ""
"`classification-attr=<name>` reads a `DictionaryAttr` named `<name>` from "
"each `cir.func` and parses it via the test-target injection helper.  Used by "
"tests to inject arbitrary classifications without depending on a real ABI "
"target."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:44
msgid "Exactly one of the two options must be set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:46
msgid "Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:55
msgid "`-cir-canonicalize`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:57
msgid "_Performs CIR canonicalization_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:59
msgid "Perform canonicalizations on CIR and removes some redundant operations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:61
msgid ""
"This pass performs basic cleanup and canonicalization transformations that "
"are not intended to affect CIR-to-source fidelity and high-level code "
"analysis passes. Example transformations performed in this pass include "
"empty scope cleanup, trivial `try` cleanup, redundant branch cleanup, etc. "
"Those more \"heavyweight\" transformations and those transformations that "
"could significantly affect CIR-to-source fidelity are performed in the `cir-"
"simplify` pass."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:69
msgid "`-cir-cxxabi-lowering`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:71
msgid "_Lower CIR according to C++ ABI requirements_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:73
msgid ""
"This pass lowers CIR operations and types that represent high-level C/C++ "
"constructs to a more fundamental form according to the target ABI "
"requirements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:77
msgid ""
"See the description of the `TargetLowering` pass for the difference between "
"this pass and the `TargetLowering` pass."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:80
msgid "`-cir-eh-abi-lowering`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:82
msgid "_Lower flattened CIR EH operations to target-specific ABI form_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:84
msgid ""
"This pass lowers the ABI-agnostic exception handling operations produced by "
"CFG flattening into an ABI-specific form. Currently only the Itanium C++ ABI "
"is implemented."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:88
msgid "For the Itanium ABI, the pass performs the following transformations:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:89
msgid "Replaces `cir.eh.initiate` with `cir.eh.inflight_exception`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:90
msgid "Replaces `cir.eh.dispatch` with `cir.eh.typeid` + comparison chains"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:91
msgid "Removes `cir.begin_cleanup` and `cir.end_cleanup` operations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:92
msgid "Replaces `cir.begin_catch` with a call to `__cxa_begin_catch`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:93
msgid "Replaces `cir.end_catch` with a call to `__cxa_end_catch`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:94
msgid "Replaces `cir.resume` with `cir.resume.flat`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:95
msgid "Sets the personality function attribute on functions that require EH"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:97
msgid ""
"If a non-Itanium ABI is specified, the pass emits a diagnostic indicating "
"that the target is not yet implemented."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:100
msgid "`-cir-flatten-cfg`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:102
msgid "_Produces flatten CFG_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:104
msgid ""
"This pass transforms CIR by inlining all the nested regions. Thus, the "
"following conditions are true after the pass applied:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:106
msgid "there are no nested regions in any function body"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:107
msgid ""
"all the blocks in a function belong to the parent region In other words, "
"this pass removes such CIR operations like IfOp, LoopOp, ScopeOp and etc. "
"and produces a flat CIR."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:111
msgid "`-cir-fold-empty-branches`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:113
msgid "_Removes blocks that contain only an unconditional branch_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:115
msgid ""
"Removes every non-entry block that has no arguments, contains only a "
"`cir.br`, and is the only predecessor of the `cir.br` destination. Each "
"predecessor of such a block branches directly to the `cir.br` destination, "
"passing the operands the `cir.br` passed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:120
msgid ""
"A `cir.br` with a `loop_id` is never removed, so loop metadata is preserved. "
"No operations other than `cir.br` are erased."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:123
msgid "`-cir-goto-solver`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:125
msgid "_Replaces goto operations with branches_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:127
msgid ""
"This pass transforms CIR and replaces goto-s with branch operations to the "
"proper blocks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:130
msgid "`-cir-hoist-allocas`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:132
msgid "_Hoist allocas to the entry of the function_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:134
msgid ""
"This pass hoist all non-dynamic allocas to the entry of the function. This "
"is helpful for later code generation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:137
msgid "`-cir-idiom-recognizer`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:139
msgid "_Raise calls to C/C++ libraries to CIR operations_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:141
msgid ""
"This pass recognizes idiomatic C++ usage and captures information about C++ "
"standard library containers, library functions calls, and types into CIR "
"operations, attributes and types."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:145
msgid "`-cir-lib-opt`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:147
msgid "_Optimize C/C++ library calls_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:149
msgid ""
"This pass applies transformations on C/C++ standard library idioms, such as "
"library function calls and structs raised to CIR operations  using the `cir-"
"idiom-recognize` pass."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:153
msgid "`-cir-lowering-prepare`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:155
msgid ""
"_Lower to more fine-grained CIR operations before lowering to other dialects_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:157
msgid ""
"This pass does preparation work for lowering to other dialects. For example, "
"it may expand the global variable initialziation in a more ABI-friendly form."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:160
msgid "`-cir-simplify`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:162
msgid "_Performs CIR simplification and code optimization_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:164
msgid ""
"The pass performs semantics-preserving code simplifications and "
"optimizations on CIR while maintaining strict program correctness."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:167
msgid ""
"Unlike the `cir-canonicalize` pass, these transformations may reduce the "
"IR's structural similarity to the original source code as a trade-off for "
"improved code quality. This can affect debugging fidelity by altering "
"intermediate representations of folded expressions, hoisted operations, and "
"other optimized constructs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:173
msgid ""
"Example transformations include ternary expression folding and code hoisting "
"while preserving program semantics."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:176
msgid "`-cir-target-lowering`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:178
msgid "_Lower CIR to a target-specific form_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:180
msgid ""
"This pass lowers CIR operations from a target-agnostic form to a target-"
"specific form without considering ABI requirements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:183
msgid ""
"CIR has three passes in its lowering pipeline that transform input CIR "
"according to target-specific requirements, scheduled in the pipeline by the "
"following order:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:187
msgid "The `TargetLowering` pass."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:188
msgid "The `CXXABILowering` pass."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:189
msgid "The `CallConvLowering` pass."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:191
msgid ""
"The `TargetLowering` pass acts more like a legalization pass. It ensures "
"every operation in CIR conforms to the target's constraints. An example "
"would be the handling of synchronization scopes of atomic operations. The "
"x86 family of targets only support a system-wide synchronization scope, thus "
"any atomic operations with a different synchronization scope would be "
"transformed to use the system-wide scope in this pass."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:198
msgid ""
"The `CXXABILowering` pass and the `CallConvLowering` pass transform the CIR "
"according to the target's ABI requirements. The former handles all ABI-"
"related lowering except for calling convention handling, which is handled "
"specifically in the latter. Example transformations that the "
"`CXXABILowering` pass could make include:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:204
msgid ""
"Replace C/C++ types that have an ABI-defined layout with more fundamental "
"types corresponding to the ABI requirements. For example, the layout of the "
"pointer-to-data-member type in C++ is ABI-defined, thus the `CXXABILowering` "
"pass would replace all occurrences of this type according to the ABI "
"requirements. With a typical target ABI, it will be replaced by the "
"`ptrdiff_t` type since this is the type most ABIs use for the layout of the "
"pointer-to-data-member type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:211
msgid ""
"Replace CIR operations that have ABI-dependent implementations with more "
"fundamental operations. For example, the `dynamic_cast` operator in C++ is "
"implemented in an ABI-dependent way, typically by calling into a library "
"function provided by the implementation. The `CXXABILowering` pass would "
"thus replace all `cir.dyn_cast` operations with corresponding library "
"function calls."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:218
msgid ""
"The `CallConvLowering` pass is dedicated to handle calling conventions. It "
"rewrites function signatures according to calling convention requirements, "
"and updates function body and call sites accordingly. For example, when "
"passing a large struct by value in C/C++, most ABIs require passing a "
"pointer to a copy of the struct instead. Thus, the `CallConvLowering` pass "
"would rewrite function signatures that take a value of a large struct type "
"to take a pointer to the struct type instead, and update the function body "
"and the call sites accordingly."
msgstr ""

