#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:1373
msgid "_Wraps C++ co_await implicit logic_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:1386
msgid ""
"The under the hood effect of using C++ `co_await expr` roughly translates to:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:1401
msgid "`cir.await` represents this logic by using 3 regions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:1402
msgid "ready: covers veto power from x.await_ready()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:1403
msgid "suspend: wraps actual x.await_suspend() logic"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:1404
msgid "resume: handles x.await_resume()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:1406
msgid ""
"Breaking this up in regions allows individual scrutiny of conditions which "
"might lead to folding some of them out. Lowerings coming out of CIR, e.g. "
"LLVM, should use the `suspend` region to track more lower level codegen "
"(e.g. intrinsic emission for coro.save/coro.suspend)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:1411
msgid "There are also 4 flavors of `cir.await` available:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:1412
msgid "`init`: compiler generated initial suspend via implicit `co_await`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:1413
msgid "`user`: also known as normal, representing a user written `co_await`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:1414
msgid "`yield`: user written `co_yield` expressions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:1415
msgid "`final`: compiler generated final suspend via implicit `co_await`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:1430
msgid ""
"Note that resulution of the common expression is assumed to happen as part "
"of the enclosing await scope."
msgstr ""

