#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:2598
msgid "`cir.cmp` (::cir::CmpOp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:2600
msgid "_Compare two values and produce a boolean result_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:2609
msgid ""
"The `cir.cmp` operation compares two operands of the same type and produces "
"a `!cir.bool` result. It supports integral, boolean, floating-point, and "
"pointer types.  Booleans (including enums with a boolean underlying type) "
"are compared as unsigned integers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:2614
msgid "The following comparison predicates are available:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:2616
msgid "`lt`: less than"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:2617
msgid "`le`: less than or equal"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:2618
msgid "`gt`: greater than"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:2619
msgid "`ge`: greater than or equal"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:2620
msgid "`eq`: equal"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:2621
msgid "`ne`: not equal"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:2622
msgid "`one`: ordered and not equal (floating-point only)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:2623
msgid "`uno`: unordered (floating-point only, true if either operand is NaN)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:2625
msgid ""
"For floating-point comparisons, the predicate follows C semantics (e.g. NaN "
"comparisons return false for all predicates except `ne`). The `one` and "
"`uno` predicates are floating-point specific: `one` is ordered not-equal "
"(false for NaN), `uno` tests if either operand is NaN."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:2630
msgid ""
"The optional `fenv` attribute describes constraints on the floating-point "
"handling of the operation. It is only valid for floating-point comparisons."
msgstr ""

