"signal mask, and other registers) in memory at `env` for use by longjmp().  "
"In this case, setjmp() returns 0. Following a successful longjmp(), "
"execution proceeds from cir.eh.setjmp with the operation yielding a  non-"
"zero value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:5106
msgid "`cir.eh.terminate` (::cir::EhTerminateOp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:5108
msgid "_Terminate due to an exception that must not escape_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:5116
msgid ""
"`cir.eh.terminate` terminates program execution when an exception reaches a "
"point from which the C++ standard does not allow it to propagate, and "
"requires `std::terminate()` to be called instead. That happens when an "
"exception is thrown while executing cleanup code during unwinding, and when "
"an exception tries to escape a function that cannot throw."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:5122
msgid ""
"This operation takes an `!cir.eh_token` and acts as a terminator. In high-"
"level CIR it appears as the only operation in the catch-all handler region "
"of the `cir.try` that wraps the body of a function that cannot throw, where "
"the token comes from the handler region's block argument. The handler is a "
"catch-all because such a function terminates on any escaping exception, and "
"it has no `cir.begin_catch` because the runtime helper this operation lowers "
"to performs the catch. After CFG flattening the token comes from a "
"`cir.eh.initiate` operation; flattening also produces this operation for "
"throwing calls found in EH cleanup regions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:5132
msgid ""
"During EH ABI lowering, this is replaced with target-specific termination "
"code. For the Itanium ABI, the `cir.eh.initiate` is lowered to "
"`cir.eh.inflight_exception` (producing an exception pointer), and the "
"`cir.eh.terminate` becomes a call to `__clang_call_terminate` with that "
"pointer, followed by an unreachable operation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:5148
msgid "And after CFG flattening:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:5166
msgid "`cir.eh.typeid` (::cir::EhTypeIdOp)"
msgstr ""

