#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6722
msgid "`cir.get_bitfield` (::cir::GetBitfieldOp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6724
msgid "_Get the information for a bitfield member_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6735
msgid ""
"The `cir.get_bitfield` operation provides a load-like access to a bit field "
"of a record."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6738
msgid ""
"It expects a name if a bit field, a pointer to a storage in the base record, "
"a type of the storage, a name of the bitfield, a size the bit field, an "
"offset of the bit field and a sign."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6742
msgid ""
"A unit attribute `volatile` can be used to indicate a volatile load of the "
"bitfield."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6748
msgid ""
"Example: Suppose we have a struct with multiple bitfields stored in "
"different members. The `cir.get_bitfield` operation gets the value of the "
"bitfield."
msgstr ""

