"signless integer attribute</td></tr>\n"
"<tr><td><code>is_volatile</code></td><td>::mlir::UnitAttr</td><td>unit "
"attribute</td></tr>\n"
"</table>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6802
msgid "`cir.get_element` (::cir::GetElementOp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6804
msgid "_Get the address of an array element_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6813
msgid ""
"The `cir.get_element` operation gets the address of a particular element "
"from the `base` array."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6816
msgid ""
"It expects a pointer to the `base` array and the `index` of the element. The "
"result pointer preserves the address space of the base pointer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:0
msgid "`base`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:0
msgid "pointer to array type"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:0
msgid "`index`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6856
msgid "`cir.get_global` (::cir::GetGlobalOp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6858
msgid "_Get the address of a global variable_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6868
msgid ""
"The `cir.get_global` operation retrieves the address pointing to a named "
"global variable. If the global variable is marked constant, writing to the "
"resulting address (such as through a `cir.store` operation) is undefined. "
"The resulting type must always be a `!cir.ptr<...>` type with the same "
"address space as the global variable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6874
msgid ""
"Addresses of thread local globals can only be retrieved if this operation is "
"marked `thread_local`, which indicates the address isn't constant."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6877
msgid ""
"The `static_local` attribute indicates that this global is a function-local "
"static variable that requires guarded initialization (e.g., C++ static local "
"variables with non-constant initializers)."
msgstr ""

