#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6969
msgid "`cir.get_method` (::cir::GetMethodOp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6971
msgid "_Resolve a method to a function pointer as callee_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6982
msgid ""
"The `cir.get_method` operation takes a pointer to method (!cir.method) and a "
"pointer to a class object (!cir.ptr<!cir.record>>) as input, and yields a "
"function pointer that points to the actual function corresponding to the "
"input method. The operation also applies any necessary adjustments to the "
"input object pointer for calling the method and yields the adjusted pointer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6982
msgid "<!cir.record>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:6989
msgid ""
"This operation is generated when calling a method through a pointer-to- "
"member-function in C++:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7000
msgid "The code above will generate CIR similar to:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7007
msgid "The method type must match the callee type. That is:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7008
msgid "The return type of the method must match the return type of the callee."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7009
msgid "The first parameter of the callee must have type `!cir.ptr<!cir.void>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7010
msgid ""
"Types of other parameters of the callee must match the method's parameters "
"after the implicit `this` pointer."
msgstr ""

