#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7029
msgid "`cir.get_runtime_member` (::cir::GetRuntimeMemberOp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7040
msgid ""
"The `cir.get_runtime_member` operation gets the address of a member from the "
"input record. The target member is given by a value of type `!"
"cir.data_member` (i.e. a pointer-to-data-member value)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7044
msgid ""
"This operation differs from `cir.get_member` in when the target member can "
"be determined. For the `cir.get_member` operation, the target member is "
"specified as a constant index so the member it returns access to is known "
"when the operation is constructed. For the `cir.get_runtime_member` "
"operation, the target member is given through a pointer-to-data-member value "
"which is unknown until the program being compiled is executed. In other "
"words, `cir.get_member` represents a normal member access through the `.` "
"operator in C/C++:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7059
msgid ""
"And `cir.get_runtime_member` represents a member access through the `.*` or "
"the `->*` operator in C++:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7072
msgid ""
"This operation expects a pointer to the base record as well as the pointer "
"to the target member."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:0
msgid "`member`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7096
msgid "`cir.global` (::cir::GlobalOp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7098
msgid "_Declare or define a global variable_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7128
msgid "The `cir.global` operation declares or defines a named global variable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7130
msgid ""
"The backing memory for the variable is allocated statically and is described "
"by the type of the variable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7133
msgid ""
"The `linkage` tracks C/C++ linkage types, currently very similar to LLVM's. "
"Symbol visibility in `sym_visibility` is defined in terms of MLIR's "
"visibility and verified to be in accordance to `linkage`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7137
msgid ""
"The `unnamed_addr` attribute indicates that the address of the global is not "
"significant, only its contents are. Such globals may be merged with other "
"globals that have identical contents. It is lowered to LLVM's `unnamed_addr` "
"(as opposed to `local_unnamed_addr`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7142
msgid ""
"The `dynamic_init_guard` attribute indicates that this global requires "
"guarded dynamic initialization via the Itanium `__cxa_guard_*` protocol "
"(e.g., C++ static local variables with non-constant initializers, or "
"namespace-scope variables with vague linkage such as weak/linkonce_odr "
"inline variables). It contains the mangled name of the guard variable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7148
msgid ""
"The `strictfp` attribute indicates that the dynamic initialization emitted "
"into the `ctorRegion`/`dtorRegion` runs under a constrained floating-point "
"environment. LoweringPrepare forwards it to the `strictfp` attribute of the "
"generated `__cxx_global_var_init` function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7153
msgid ""
"The `init_priority` attribute records the priority specified by a C++ "
"`init_priority` attribute on the source variable declaration. "
"LoweringPrepare uses it to place the dynamic initializer emitted from "
"`ctorRegion` into a priority-specific `_GLOBAL__I_<priority>` function "
"instead of the default `_GLOBAL__sub_I_*` function."
msgstr ""

