"attribute</td></tr>\n"
"</table>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7254
msgid "`cir.if` (::cir::IfOp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7256
msgid "_The if-then-else operation_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7258
msgid ""
"The `cir.if` operation represents an if-then-else construct for "
"conditionally executing two regions of code. The operand is a `cir.bool` "
"type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7283
msgid ""
"`cir.if` defines no values and the 'else' can be omitted. The if/else "
"regions must be terminated. If the region has only one block, the terminator "
"can be left out, and `cir.yield` terminator will be inserted implictly. "
"Otherwise, the region must be explicitly terminated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7300
msgid "`cir.inc` (::cir::IncOp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7302
msgid "_Increment an integer by one_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7311
msgid ""
"The `cir.inc` operation increments the operand by one. The operand and "
"result must have the same type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7344
msgid "`cir.indirect_br` (::cir::IndirectBrOp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7346
msgid "_Indirect branch_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7359
msgid ""
"The `cir.indirectbr` operation represents an indirect branch to one of "
"several possible successor blocks. The target block is computed from the "
"value of the given address operand."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7363
msgid ""
"This operation is typically generated when handling constructs like the GCC "
"extension `&&label` combined with an indirect `goto *ptr;`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7366
msgid ""
"The `poison` attribute is used to mark an `indirectbr` that was created but "
"is known to be invalid, for instance when a label address was taken but no "
"indirect branch was ever emitted."
msgstr ""

