#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7910
msgid "`cir.lifetime.end` (::cir::LifetimeEndOp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7912
msgid ""
"_Marks the end of the lifetime of a variable produced by a cir.alloca "
"operation_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7920
msgid ""
"The `cir.lifetime.end` operation marks the end of the lifetime of the "
"storage pointed to by `$ptr`. After this operation the underlying storage is "
"considered dead, and the optimizer is free to reuse the storage for other "
"purposes, until a subsequent `cir.lifetime.start` on the same pointer "
"revives it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7926 ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7970
msgid ""
"The `cir.scope` is the operation that models the block scope of the C/C++ "
"source. Once ClangIR is no longer structured, `cir.scope` can no longer "
"express the lifetime of a local variable. This happens, for example, after "
"`FlattenCFG`, where `cir.scope` regions are dissolved into plain basic "
"blocks, or after `HoistAllocas`, where an alloca is moved to the function "
"entry so that its position no longer reflects the scope it was declared in. "
"In that form, these lifetime markers are what delimit the beginning and end "
"of a variable's lifetime."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7935
msgid ""
"The verifier requires `$ptr` to be produced by a `cir.alloca`. "
"`cir.lifetime.end` should be preceded by a matching `cir.lifetime.start` on "
"the same pointer on every control-flow path that reaches it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7939
msgid "This operation corresponds to the LLVM intrinsic `llvm.lifetime.end`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7954
msgid "`cir.lifetime.start` (::cir::LifetimeStartOp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7956
msgid ""
"_Marks the start of the lifetime of a variable produced by a cir.alloca "
"operation_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7964
msgid ""
"The `cir.lifetime.start` operation marks the beginning of the lifetime of "
"the storage pointed to by `$ptr`. Between this operation and a matching "
"`cir.lifetime.end` on the same pointer, the underlying storage is considered "
"live; outside that range it is considered dead, and the optimizer is free to "
"reuse the storage for other purposes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7979
msgid ""
"The verifier requires `$ptr` to be produced by a `cir.alloca`. For the "
"lifetime to be meaningful, a matching `cir.lifetime.end` on the same pointer "
"should follow on every control-flow path. This is different from LLVM, where "
"an `llvm.lifetime.start` may appear without a matching `llvm.lifetime.end` "
"-- there the storage is also implicitly marked dead when the function "
"returns (see the [LLVM LangRef](https://llvm.org/docs/LangRef.html#int-"
"lifestart))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7987
msgid "This operation corresponds to the LLVM intrinsic `llvm.lifetime.start`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:8002
