#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:8081
msgid "`cir.load` (::cir::LoadOp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:8083
msgid "_Load value from memory adddress_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:8098
msgid ""
"`cir.load` reads a value (lvalue to rvalue conversion) given an address "
"backed up by a `cir.ptr` type. A unit attribute `deref` can be used to mark "
"the resulting value as used by another operation to dereference a pointer. A "
"unit attribute `volatile` can be used to indicate a volatile loading. Load "
"can be marked atomic by using `atomic(<mem_order>)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:8104 ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:10541
msgid ""
"`alignment` can be used to specify an alignment that's different from the "
"default, which is computed from `result`'s type ABI data layout."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:8107
msgid ""
"A unit attribute `invariant` can be used to indicate that the loaded memory "
"never changes, mapping to LLVM IR's `!invariant.load` metadata."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:8131
msgid "Interfaces: `InferTypeOpInterface`, `PromotableMemOpInterface`"
msgstr ""

