msgid "CIR type that is used for the vptr member of C++ objects"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:12598
msgid "`cir.vtable.get_type_info` (::cir::VTableGetTypeInfoOp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:12600
msgid "_Get the address of the type_info from the vtable_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:12608
msgid ""
"The `vtable.get_type_info` operation retreives the address of the dynamic "
"type_info/rtti object from an object's vtable. This is an ABI independent "
"abstraction of this operation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:12612
msgid ""
"The `vptr` operand must be a `!cir.vptr` value, which would have been "
"returned by a previous call to `cir.vtable.get_vptr`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:12615
msgid "The return type is a loadable pointer to a `type_info` struct."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:0
msgid "`vptr`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:12646
msgid "`cir.vtable.get_virtual_fn_addr` (::cir::VTableGetVirtualFnAddrOp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:12648
msgid "_Get a the address of a virtual function pointer_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:12657
msgid ""
"The `vtable.get_virtual_fn_addr` operation retrieves the address of a "
"virtual function pointer from an object's vtable (__vptr). This is an "
"abstraction to perform the basic pointer arithmetic to get the address of "
"the virtual function pointer, which can then be loaded and called."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:12663
msgid ""
"The `vptr` operand must be a `!cir.ptr<!cir.vptr>` value, which would have "
"been returned by a previous call to `cir.vtable.get_vptr`. The `index` "
"operand is an index of the virtual function in the vtable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:12667
msgid "The return type is a pointer-to-pointer to the function type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:12710
msgid "`cir.vtable.get_vptr` (::cir::VTableGetVPtrOp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:12712
msgid "_Get a the address of the vtable pointer for an object_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:12720
msgid ""
"The `vtable.get_vptr` operation retrieves the address of the vptr for a C++ "
"object. This operation requires that the object pointer points to the start "
"of a complete object. (TODO: Describe how we get that). The vptr will always "
"be at offset zero in the object, but this operation is more explicit about "
"what is being retrieved than a direct bitcast."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:12726
msgid "The return type is always `!cir.ptr<!cir.vptr>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:0
msgid "pointer to vptr type"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:12754
msgid "`cir.vtt.address_point` (::cir::VTTAddrPointOp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:12756
msgid "_Get the VTT address point_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:12768
msgid ""
"The `vtt.address_point` operation retrieves an element from the virtual "
"table table (VTT), which is the address point of a C++ vtable. In virtual "
"inheritance, a set of internal `__vptr` members for an object are "
"initialized by this operation, which assigns an element from the VTT. The "
"initialization order is as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:12774
msgid ""
"The complete object constructors and destructors find the VTT, via the "
"mangled name of the VTT global variable. They pass the address of the "
"subobject's sub-VTT entry in the VTT as a second parameter when calling the "
"base object constructors and destructors. The base object constructors and "
"destructors use the address passed to initialize the primary virtual pointer "
"and virtual pointers that point to the classes which either have virtual "
"bases or override virtual functions with a virtual step."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:12783
msgid ""
"The first parameter is either the mangled name of VTT global variable or the "
"address of the subobject's sub-VTT entry in the VTT. The second parameter "
"`offset` provides a virtual step to adjust to the actual address point of "
"the vtable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:12788
msgid "The return type is always a `!cir.ptr<!cir.ptr<void>>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:12800
msgid "Or:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:12814
msgid ""
"<table>\n"
"<tr><th>Attribute</th><th>MLIR Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n"
"<tr><td><code>name</code></td><td>::mlir::FlatSymbolRefAttr</td><td>flat "
"symbol reference attribute</td></tr>\n"
"<tr><td><code>offset</code></td><td>::mlir::IntegerAttr</td><td>32-bit "
"signless integer attribute</td></tr>\n"
"</table>\n"
msgstr ""

