#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:12834
msgid "`cir.while` (::cir::WhileOp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:12836
msgid "_C/C++ while loop_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:12845
msgid "Represents a C/C++ while loop. It consists of two or three regions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:12850
msgid ""
"`cleanup`: optional region that runs on every per-iteration exit edge "
"(condition-false exit, end-of-iteration, break/continue, and EH unwinding "
"when the cleanup kind includes EH). This is used to destroy a condition "
"variable whose lifetime is a single iteration. When present, it carries a "
"cleanup kind matching `cir.cleanup.scope` (`normal` or `all`). Note that a "
"`DoWhileOp` cannot contain a `cleanup` region."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:12890
msgid "`cir.xor` (::cir::XorOp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:12892
msgid "_Bitwise XOR_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:12900
msgid ""
"The `cir.xor` operation performs a bitwise XOR on integer operands. Both "
"operands and the result must have the same integer type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:12910
msgid "Traits: `Commutative`, `SameOperandsAndResultType`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:12931
msgid "`cir.yield` (::cir::YieldOp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:12933
msgid "_Represents the default branching behaviour of a region_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:12941
msgid ""
"The `cir.yield` operation terminates regions on different CIR operations, "
"and it is used to represent the default branching behaviour of a region. "
"Said branching behaviour is determinted by the parent operation. For "
"example, a yield in a `switch-case` region implies a fallthrough, while a "
"yield in a `cir.if` region implies a branch to the exit block, and so on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:12948
msgid ""
"In some cases, it might yield an SSA value and the semantics of how the "
"values are yielded is defined by the parent operation. For example, a "
"`cir.ternary` operation yields a value from one of its regions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:12952
msgid ""
"As a general rule, `cir.yield` must be explicitly used whenever a region has "
"more than one block and no terminator, or within `cir.switch` regions not "
"`cir.return` terminated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:12986
msgid ""
"Traits: `HasParent<ArrayCtor, ArrayDtor, AwaitOp, CaseOp, CleanupScopeOp, "
"CoroutineOp, DoWhileOp, ForOp, GlobalOp, IfOp, LocalInitOp, "
"RegisterExitDtorOp, ScopeOp, SwitchOp, TernaryOp, TryOp, WhileOp>`, "
"`ReturnLike`, `Terminator`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:12988
msgid ""
"Interfaces: `NoMemoryEffect (MemoryEffectOpInterface)`, "
"`RegionBranchTerminatorOpInterface`"
msgstr ""

