msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:14864
msgid ""
"_LangOptions and CodeGenOptions facts that post-CIRGen lowering consumes_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:14887
msgid ""
"Serializes the subset of `clang::LangOptions` and `clang::CodeGenOptions` "
"that post-CIRGen lowering reads, as plain data, so a reloaded `.cir` module "
"lowers the same way it was compiled without a live `clang::LangOptions` or "
"`clang::CodeGenOptions`. Only flags with no triple/module representation "
"live here; target-derived facts (size_t width, CXXABI, fp formats, etc.) are "
"rebuilt from `cir.triple` instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:14894
msgid ""
"The following fields come from `LangOptions`.  Each bool field mirrors the "
"like-named `LangOptions` member: `exceptions`, `threadsafe_statics`, `cuda`, "
"`cuda_is_device`, `hip`, `hlsl`, `gpu_rdc`, `openmp` (`LangOpts.OpenMP != "
"0`; only its on/off state matters), and `openmp_is_target_device`. "
"`clang_abi_compat` is an `i32` mirroring `LangOptions::ClangABI`; it is an "
"`i32` rather than a CIR enum because `ClangABI` gains an enumerator every "
"Clang release (see `clang/Basic/ABIVersions.def`), and the ordinal round-"
"trips fine within a single toolchain. `no_trapping_math` is true when "
"`LangOptions::getDefaultExceptionMode()` is `FPE_Ignore`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:14905
msgid ""
"The following fields come from `CodeGenOptions`. `enable_noundef_attrs` "
"mirrors `CodeGenOptions::EnableNoundefAttrs`, which calling convention "
"lowering reads when it decides whether an argument is `noundef`. "
"`ssp_buffer_size` mirrors `CodeGenOptions::SSPBufferSize`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:14911
msgid ""
"`LowerToLLVM` turns `no_trapping_math` and `ssp_buffer_size` into the `\"no-"
"trapping-math\"` and `\"stack-protector-buffer-size\"` LLVM function "
"attributes of every function not marked `runtime_func`. A `strictfp` "
"function does not get `\"no-trapping-math\"`, since a pragma such as "
"`float_control(except, on)` can make its FP operations observe exceptions "
"even when the TU-wide default ignores them."
msgstr ""

