msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16138
msgid "_CIR matrix type_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16150
msgid ""
"The `!cir.matrix` type represents a fixed-size 2-dimensional matrix. It "
"takes three parameters: the element type, the number of rows, and columns."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16162
msgid ""
"The `element-type` must be a scalar CIR type. Zero-sized matrices are not "
"allowed. The `row` and `column` count must be a positive integer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:0
msgid "element_type"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:0
msgid "any cir boolean, integer, floating point type"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:0
msgid "num_rows"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:0
msgid "num_columns"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16180
msgid "MethodType"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16182
msgid "_CIR type that represents C++ pointer-to-member-function type_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16193
msgid ""
"`cir.method` models the pointer-to-member-function type in C++. The layout "
"of this type is ABI-dependent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:0
msgid "member_func_ty"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:0
msgid "`cir::FuncType`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16203
msgid "PointerType"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16205
msgid "_CIR pointer type_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16216
msgid ""
"The `!cir.ptr` type is a typed pointer type. It is used to represent "
"pointers to objects in C/C++. The type of the pointed-to object is given by "
"the `pointee` parameter. The `addrSpace` parameter is an optional address "
"space attribute that specifies the address space of the pointer. If not "
"specified, the pointer is assumed to be in the default address space."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16222
msgid ""
"The `!cir.ptr` type can point to any CIR type, including fundamental types, "
"records, arrays, vectors, functions, and other pointers. It can also point "
"to incomplete types, such as incomplete records."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:0
msgid "pointee"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:0
msgid "addrSpace"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:0
msgid "`mlir::ptr::MemorySpaceAttrInterface`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16243
msgid "SingleType"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16245
msgid "_CIR single-precision 32-bit float type_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16247
msgid "Syntax: `!cir.float`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16249
msgid ""
"A 32-bit floating-point type whose format is IEEE-754 `binary32`.  It "
"represents the types `float`, `_Float32`, and `std::float32_t` in C and C++."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16253
msgid "StructType"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16255
msgid "_CIR struct/class type_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16257
msgid ""
"Each unique clang::RecordDecl with struct or class kind is mapped to a "
"`cir.struct` type.  Any object in C/C++ that has a struct or class type will "
"have a `!cir.struct` in CIR."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16261 ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16317
msgid "There are three possible formats:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16263 ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16319
msgid "Identified and complete: unique name and a known body."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16264 ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16320
msgid "Identified and incomplete: unique name and unknown body."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16265 ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16321
msgid "Anonymous: no name and a known body."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16267
msgid ""
"Typically, the full data size of a struct object is that which is calculated "
"by adding the aligned sizes of all the members. However, note that there is "
"one exception to this Flexible Array Members. When the last element is an "
"array type of size zero(in CIR), this represents the C/C++ concept of "
"'flexible array member', where as long as the type is allocated properly (or "
"a global constant), an access through the array member may access outside of "
"its bounds. This is necessary to represent C/C++ semantics."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16275
msgid ""
"The optional `class` keyword distinguishes C++ class declarations from plain "
"struct declarations.  Both are semantically identical; the keyword preserves "
"the original source spelling."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16279
msgid ""
"Every member has a kind, described by `CIR_RecordMemberKind`, saying what it "
"holds, and every member is spelled with its mark."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:0
msgid "incomplete"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:0
msgid "packed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:0
msgid "member_kinds"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:0
msgid "`::llvm::ArrayRef<cir::RecordMemberKind>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:0
msgid "is_class"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16309
msgid "UnionType"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16311
msgid "_CIR union type_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16313
msgid ""
"Each unique clang::RecordDecl with union kind is mapped to a `cir.union` "
"type.  Any object in C/C++ that has a union type will have a `!cir.union` in "
"CIR."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16323
msgid ""
"Padded unions carry an explicit tail-padding type to ensure the LLVM struct "
"that models the union has the correct byte size.  The padding type is `!u8i` "
"or an array of `!u8i`.  That slot is separate from the per-member kinds "
"described by `CIR_RecordMemberKind`, which say what each variant holds.  The "
"parser rejects a mark on that slot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:0
msgid "padding"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16353
msgid "VPtrType"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16355
msgid "_CIR type that is used for the vptr member of C++ objects_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16357
msgid "Syntax: `!cir.vptr`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16359
msgid ""
"`cir.vptr` is a special type used as the type for the vptr member of a C++ "
"object. This avoids using arbitrary pointer types to declare vptr values and "
"allows stronger type-based checking for operations that use or provide "
"access to the vptr."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16364
msgid ""
"This type will be the element type of the 'vptr' member of structures that "
"require a vtable pointer. The `cir.vtable.address_point` operation returns "
"this type. The `cir.vtable.get_vptr` operations returns a pointer to this "
"type. This pointer may be passed to the `cir.vtable.get_virtual_fn_addr` "
"operation to get the address of a virtual function pointer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16370
msgid ""
"The pointer may also be cast to other pointer types in order to perform "
"pointer arithmetic based on information encoded in the AST layout to get the "
"offset from a pointer to a dynamic object to the base object pointer, the "
"base object offset value from the vtable, or the type information entry for "
"an object. TODO: We should have special operations to do that too."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16378
msgid "VectorType"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16380
msgid "_CIR vector type_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16382
msgid ""
"The `!cir.vector` type represents a one-dimensional vector. It takes two "
"parameters: the element type and an element count, which records both the "
"known minimum number of elements and whether the vector is scalable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16395
msgid ""
"The `element-type` must be a scalar CIR type. Zero-sized vectors are not "
"allowed. The `size` must be a positive integer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16405
msgid ""
"A fixed-length vector of `!cir.bool` is packed one bit per element, and its "
"size is rounded up to a power of two of at least one byte, so `!cir.vector<4 "
"x !cir.bool>` occupies one byte and `!cir.vector<17 x !cir.bool>` occupies "
"four."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16410
msgid "Scalable vectors are indicated by enclosing size in square brackets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:0
msgid "`llvm::ElementCount`"
msgstr ""

